<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12032" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέχθ-ομαι</span></b> , later form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεχθάνομαι,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			7.45
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Lyc.
			116
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			5.176
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Mel.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>Marc.</u>
			22
		</span></i>, etc.; for in <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Hipp.</u>
			1260
		</span></i>
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάχθομαι</span> is the better reading; and
		the inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέχθεσθαι</span> freq. found in codd. should
		be written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεχθέσθαι, ξφ.
		ἀπεχθάνομαι.</span></div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
